this procedure yielded a predicted thermostabilization with respect to WT BsLipA for 75 out of the 522 mutations (\(\sim\!14\%\)) investigated. In order to further reduce the number of mutations for experimental validation only the mutation with the highest \(\Delta T_{\mathrm{p}}\) was chosen from all mutations with \(\Delta T_{\mathrm{p}}>1\,\mathrm{K}\) at a weak spot. The sole exception is G104 located in the active site, for which two mutations were chosen. This resulted in twelve lipase variants of which the most are associated with weak spot residues on helix αB identified during the late transition T4 (Table 2; S1 Fig).
As a negative control, we also predicted 10 variants with negative \(\Delta T_{\mathrm{p}}\), i.e., where a mutation according to the thermal unfolding simulations leads to a decrease in thermostability with respect to WT (S1 Table). Six of these mutations were chosen from the above analyses of 522 variants such that they have the most negative \(\Delta T_{\mathrm{p}}\); four were chosen with the most negative \(\Delta T_{\mathrm{p}}\) from analyses of variants with a mutation not at a weak spot.
